    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's the thing, I don't want to build something new. everything feels like a consolation prize. when u spend your whole life being \"the athlete,\" and that's gone... what's actually left? it's like the story is already over, and i'm just stuck in the credits rolling on a blank screen. it doesn't feel like a \"new space,\" it just feels like things are finished.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's completely understandable to feel that the story is over when your identity was so tied to that one pursuit. Being \"the athlete\" was a role, and now you're facing the terrifying reality of being just *you*, which is a much harder thing to navigate. Instead of trying to build something new, maybe just focus on letting the old narrative fade, allowing yourself to simply *be* without the pressure of a plot.",
      "source": "target",
